Nice collection you have there.

No point in advancing your twoweapon skill past your primary weapon 
skill. The skill used is the lower of your twoweapon skill and your 
primary weapon skill, so it won't be more than 'skilled' for you anyway. 
(a -5 to hit and +0 dmg bonus). The secondary weapon doesn't even have a 
tohit roll; it hits automatically if your primary does (so you want your 
more skilled weapon in the primary slot, if both aren't artifacts).

 From what I've seen, both Frosty and Grayswandir are both notably 
better than Stormbringer. I think Grayswandir is better; all demons but 
the riders are silver hating and will take +d20 dmg. Also, Frostbrand 
freezes potions sometimes, which is annoying. Grayswandir will do better 
against the riders (riders are resistant to everything, so no frost). A 
+7 silver saber is probably the best secondary weapon. A longsword (or 
katana) would be better if you never fought silver-hating creatures, but 
you meet a lot of demons and vampires. Also, shades can only be hurt by 
silver. If it's already +7, that's just another reason to keep it.

Of course, those daggers will probably serve you better than anything. 
Use them constantly. I'd keep more than 12 out at a time, if you can 
afford the weight. Also, bless 'em if they're not.

